[quote="phantaskippy"]

Deadline was trying to destroy weak points on Earth in order to save the people of Earth, so they wouldn&#39;t die like his people did.Chokepoint goes through similar changes when she merges with his tech.When they fight Progeny they pull even more at the timelines that already were messed up.I think that events on Earth are destabilizing the fabric of reality, and Oblivaeon is coming to fix the problem. &nbsp;We are the rats that chewed through a power cord and shorted out the fuses. &nbsp;The maintenance guy wakes up, finds a mess and tries to clean it up only to have the rats gang up and call their friends who chew through the freaking walls to chase him out.Now the Land lord is coming over to exterminate the problem.&nbsp;

[/quote]

&nbsp;

I like this metaphor a lot, very evocative...!

[quote="Foote"]

Could Cap. Cosbys brother be the Scion who will aid our heroes in the final battle?

[/quote]

Could be, but the way he turns hero in the promo makes that feel kind of weird. &nbsp;Also, every time we see him, its associated with green energy, and while that could certainly be changed, it seems weird to me.&nbsp;

I could totally see it being Voss, as some folks have said.

My big suspect is Visionary. &nbsp;She keeps being squirrely about Progeny, We&#39;ve seen her use that pink energy before, and her body is currently being occupied by Dark visionary (at least during progeny&#39;s fight), but we see her back in her original costume on Cerebral Hermorrage, where she is specifically fighting the Aeon men. We also know that (dark) visionary is pretty capable of being snide and contemptuous, and regular visionary occasionally comes off as being distant. &nbsp;I could see a Scion empowered version having the worst qualities of both. &nbsp;

